{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038278-proximi-dynasty-the-mist-blinded","id":1038278,"title":"Proximi Dynasty: The Mist Blinded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-25T22:51:24-08:00","id":1038278,"title":"Proximi Dynasty: The Mist Blinded","content":"First crack at Proximi write up, wanted more Myrddin/Walkers in the Mist related shenanigans for my chronicle. I need to write more in the way of background fluff but I'm coming down with monitor induced weariness and wanted to post something before turning in. Comments and Criticisms gratefully revived. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Proximi Dynasty: The Mist Blinded</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>You know he was one of us right? The big guy with the pointy hat, capital M? Yeah of course he was a real Awakened. The Deacon supposedly even has a Grimoire he wrote. Arthur and all that other stuff? That stuff is kinda is up for debate, it sorta did happen and always will but then it sorta never did happen at all. Talking about timeline editing makes my head hurt. But the man himself was totally one hundred percent legit. </i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>You want proof? Argh alright then you know the sleepwalkers who help run the local Crytopoly? Yeah the ones with the freaky eyes, they\u2019re his blood. Story goes He falls in love with this girl, but She's terrified of being with him because He knows the Art right and She\u2019ll never know if She\u2019s with Him cause She wants to be or if He\u2019s making Her want to. So He promises to teach Her all He knows and that way they can be together, course soon as She\u2019s learnt all can She binds Him to a cave or a tree or something for the rest of time while she swans off to be remembered as the lady of the lake. What she didn't know at the time was that she already had a bun in the oven. They\u2019re still with the Order after all this time and just between you and me; if one of them tells you Its gonna rain tomorrow pack an umbrella, you dig? </i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nicknames:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Crystal Balls (informal and sometimes derogatorily), Myriddingwaed (among the Silver Ladder)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Appearance:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Mist Blinded run the gamut of physical traits with exception of the eyes; each of the Dynasty who manifest the blessings of the lineage are beleaguered by the constant gathering of the Mists within their sight. The Mists become visible as a cloudy film over the eyes, mistakable for glaucoma or cataracts, it\u2019s almost imperceptible at first but thickens with time until in advanced age they are left with opaque orbs bereft of iris and pupil.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After death the eyes of the Proximus crystallize into moonstone like gems, these are morbid yet highly prized as sacraments for scrying or divination spells.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Path:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Arcanthus</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blessings (Fate, Space, Time): </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Fate -</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reaching the Outmost Eddies (\u25cf), Serendipity (\u25cf), Exceptional Luck (\u25cf\u25cf), Lucky Number (\u25cf\u25cf), Shifting the Odds (\u25cf\u25cf), Superlative Luck (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Space - </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correspondence (\u25cf), The Outward and Inward Eye (\u25cf), Scrying (\u25cf\u25cf)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Time - </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Divination (\u25cf), Perfect Timing (\u25cf), Postcognition (\u25cf), Choose the Thread (\u25cf\u25cf), Hung Spell (\u25cf\u25cf), Veil of Moments (\u25cf\u25cf), Shifting Sands (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf), Weight of Years (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Curse: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From the first manifestation of their Blessing the proximus\u2019 eyes begin to slowly fill and cloud over with the Mists. The Mists are ever shifting and coalescing into omens of the future. The omens that the Mists reveal are never simply content to be witnessed. The omens demand to be interpreted and foretold lest they completely consume the sight of the proximus. The proximus must routinely engage in some form of divination or augury to clear away the Mists. Tea leaves, I-ching and cartomancy ect will all work but crystal gazing is a recurring favorite with many finding it just \u201cfeels right\u201d. What is more the results of the fortune telling must be shared with at least one other person to satisfy the needs of the curse.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Persistent -</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Mist Blinded suffers a -2 to any rolls that rely on vision</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Beat -</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Mist Blinded fails a roll penalised by the curse</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Severe -</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Should the proximus go a full 24 hours without some form of divination or suffers a Paradox they take the full effects of the Blinded Tilt as their vision is completely overcome by the Mists </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Resolution - </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The proximus gives prophesy to the omens in the form of a cruel malediction upon a friend or loved one. The malediction must be delivered verbally, clearly and in person during which The Mist Blinded expends all remaining willpower. For the a number of days equal to the proximus\u2019 willpower dots any failures on behalf of the subject of the malediction are treated as dramatic failures. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">experiencing periods of sensory deprivation, playing a game of chance, walking or traveling with no destination in mind.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T00:03:18-08:00","id":1038289,"title":"","content":"Neat. Don't recall the exact mechanics a dynasty is supposed to follow, but this all looks nice and usable. I think I could even adapt this concept to a character I've been pondering about.<br /> <br /> Do you have any sample story hooks for these guys?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T19:45:06-08:00","id":1038711,"title":"","content":"I like this. I like it a lot. *Idly yoinks for game play*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T01:05:52-08:00","id":1038799,"title":"","content":"Looks nice, and I do love to see people post custom stuff for us to read. Hence my actual love for CoD over WoD as it stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:16:19-08:00","id":1042146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038278-proximi-dynasty-the-mist-blinded?p=1038289#post1038289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do you have any sample story hooks for these guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>well since you asked;<ul><li>A local Therach has employed the assistance of one of the Myrrdingwaed for years and frequently reaped the benefits. Last week however the Proximus got into an accident, nothing too serious but they were laid up in the hospital for a couple of days and their curse has kicked up into severe mode. The Therach needs their Crystal Ball working again and the Proximus desperatly need their eyesight back. The Therach is looking for someone to willingly take the Proximus' Malection and is willing to pay big in return; anything access to hallows, grimories, artifacts to helping twist some elbows and cut some red tape with the local Consilim/ Ladder Caucus. The Therach even is able to use Space to shift sympathetic links onto the characters so they can suffer the Malediction. How bad can bad luck be and is it worth it?</li> <li>Someone or something is stalking the Mist Blinded for their eyes. The Moonstone like gems they become after death are known for their use as a sacrement for scrying and divination spells but suddenly the local caucuses are awash in rumours for other uses for these morbid trophies. Some say that crushing them onto a doorway or mirror can create iris' to other realms others say that after being properly prepared and consumed they can bestow extraordinary luck or terrible misfortune. Where did all these rumours come from, is there any truth to them, who is collecting all the eyes and what do they want with them?</li> <li>That there is some connection between The Mist Blinded and the Walkers in the Mist legacy is an open secret amongst the Ladder and the Mysterium. A much more closely guarded secret is that the Mists that gather in the eyes of the Proximi can also be found their Oneiroi. Trace these Mists back deep enough and far enough into the proximus' oneiros and it is said you will find a doorway slightly ajar from where the Mists seep into the soul of The Mist Blinded. Close it fully and the proximus will lose access to their blessings but also freed from the maddening omens that cloud their sight. Open it wide and you could bodily enter the realm of Unknown Destiny, otherwise jealously guarded by the Walker Legacy, the rewards could be untold so could the damage done to the Proximus as the trickle of the Mists become a flood.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}